IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rtw-dates`
IMPORT `rtw-core`
IMPORT `rtw-seat`
IMPORT `rtw-seat-employer`

-- Return to Work Act 2014 (SA) -- cases for the employer's seat (rtw-seat-employer.l4), with MIRROR cases: the same facts
-- asked from the employer's seat and from the worker's seat (rtw-seat.l4), with answers that agree. The claim-forwarding
-- and suitable-work rules are also traced on the day counts the two seats' date answers give.
--
-- The employer is Mia's: a warehouse company in Adelaide, registered with ReturnToWorkSA and not self-insured. Mia (born
-- 14 May 1990) is injured on Monday 2 March 2026; the employer receives her notice of injury that day and her claim on
-- Tuesday 10 March 2026; her incapacity first occurs on 3 March 2026. Monday 9 March 2026 is Adelaide Cup Day (one weekday
-- public holiday where it falls in a period). ILLUSTRATIVE CPI figures 125.4 and 100.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text, with the arithmetic in the comment above it.

-- The day inside a forwarding answer (a helper for the traces; no rule).
GIVEN a IS A `Forwarding answer`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day in` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `the employer must forward it to the Corporation no later than` d THEN d
    OTHERWISE `the calendar date` 1 1 2000

GIVEN a IS A `Tribunal window answer`
GIVETH A DATE
`the Tribunal day in` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `the worker may apply to the Tribunal no later than` d THEN d
    OTHERWISE `the calendar date` 1 1 2000

§ `Who is my worker?`

#ASSERT `Is this person my worker` TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 5 classes` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 6 classes` 125.4 100
-- Mirror: Mia, an employee.
#ASSERT (`Is this person my worker` TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 5 classes` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 6 classes` 125.4 100) EQUALS (`Am I a worker` TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 5 classes` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 6 classes` 125.4 100)
-- Mirror: a delivery rider the business engages (a worker under reg 5(1)(e)).
#ASSERT `Is this person my worker` FALSE FALSE FALSE `driving or riding a vehicle other than a commercial motor vehicle to carry goods` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 6 classes` 125.4 100
#ASSERT (`Is this person my worker` FALSE FALSE FALSE `driving or riding a vehicle other than a commercial motor vehicle to carry goods` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 6 classes` 125.4 100) EQUALS (`Am I a worker` FALSE FALSE FALSE `driving or riding a vehicle other than a commercial motor vehicle to carry goods` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 6 classes` 125.4 100)
-- Mirror: an employed owner-driver of a commercial van (excluded by reg 6(4)).
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is this person my worker` TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 5 classes` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `a driver carrying goods in a commercial motor vehicle the driver owns, leases or hires` 125.4 100))
#ASSERT (`Is this person my worker` TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 5 classes` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `a driver carrying goods in a commercial motor vehicle the driver owns, leases or hires` 125.4 100) EQUALS (`Am I a worker` TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 5 classes` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 0 1 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `a driver carrying goods in a commercial motor vehicle the driver owns, leases or hires` 125.4 100)
-- Mirror: the cleaner averaging $140 a month on a 3-month contract (a worker with the CPI at 125.4).
#ASSERT (`Is this person my worker` FALSE FALSE FALSE `cleaning work other than window cleaning` TRUE TRUE FALSE 420 0 0 3 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 6 classes` 125.4 100) EQUALS (`Am I a worker` FALSE FALSE FALSE `cleaning work other than window cleaning` TRUE TRUE FALSE 420 0 0 3 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of the regulation 6 classes` 125.4 100)
-- s 4(4): a principal whose contractor is not registered is taken to be the employer. Mirror.
#ASSERT `Am I taken to be the employer of my contractor's workers` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT (`Am I taken to be the employer of my contractor's workers` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS (`Is the principal taken to be my employer` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT (`Am I taken to be the employer of my contractor's workers` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS (`Is the principal taken to be my employer` TRUE TRUE)
-- s 7. Mirror: Mia's back; a psychiatric injury mainly from reasonable performance management.
#ASSERT `Is this injury a work injury in my employment` `a physical injury` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT (`Is this injury a work injury in my employment` `a physical injury` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS (`Is my injury a work injury` `a physical injury` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT (`Is this injury a work injury in my employment` `a psychiatric injury` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS (`Is my injury a work injury` `a psychiatric injury` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT (NOT (`Is this injury a work injury in my employment` `a psychiatric injury` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))

§ `Notices and claims`

-- s 16(4), reg 11. Mirror: notice by email to the business address.
#ASSERT `Is this notice taken to have been given to me` `by email to an address the employer uses in the ordinary course of business`
#ASSERT (`Is this notice taken to have been given to me` `by email to an address the employer uses in the ordinary course of business`) EQUALS (`Is my notice taken to have been given to my employer` `by email to an address the employer uses in the ordinary course of business`)
#ASSERT (`Is this notice taken to have been given to me` `in some other way`) EQUALS (`Is my notice taken to have been given to my employer` `in some other way`)
-- s 16(6): notice received Monday 2 March 2026; with Adelaide Cup Day, the 5th business day after is Tuesday 10 March.
#ASSERT `By when must I send a copy of the notice of injury` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) 1 FALSE EQUALS `the employer must forward it to the Corporation no later than` (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I send a copy of the notice of injury` (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) 1 TRUE EQUALS `no duty to forward: the employer is a self-insured employer`
-- s 30(5): Mia's claim, received Tuesday 10 March 2026: forward by Tuesday 17 March. Mirror with Mia's question.
#ASSERT `By when must I forward this claim` TRUE (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) 0 FALSE EQUALS `the employer must forward it to the Corporation no later than` (`the calendar date` 17 3 2026)
#ASSERT (`By when must I forward this claim` TRUE (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) 0 FALSE) EQUALS (`By when must my employer forward my claim` TRUE (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) 0 FALSE)
-- Received on Monday 9 March, Adelaide Cup Day itself (finding 19, corrected): the day of receipt is not one of the 5
-- business days after it, so its holiday is not in the period (0 holidays): 10, 11, 12, 13, 16 March, so Monday 16
-- March. (This case once passed 1 holiday and expected Tuesday 17 March, a day late.) Mirror.
#ASSERT `By when must I forward this claim` TRUE (`the calendar date` 9 3 2026) 0 FALSE EQUALS `the employer must forward it to the Corporation no later than` (`the calendar date` 16 3 2026)
#ASSERT (`By when must I forward this claim` TRUE (`the calendar date` 9 3 2026) 0 FALSE) EQUALS (`By when must my employer forward my claim` TRUE (`the calendar date` 9 3 2026) 0 FALSE)
-- Mirror: self-insured; and a worker not employed when the incapacity began (the claim goes to ReturnToWorkSA).
#ASSERT (`By when must I forward this claim` TRUE (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) 0 TRUE) EQUALS (`By when must my employer forward my claim` TRUE (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) 0 TRUE)
#ASSERT (`By when must I forward this claim` FALSE (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) 0 FALSE) EQUALS (`By when must my employer forward my claim` FALSE (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) 0 FALSE)
#ASSERT `By when must I forward this claim` FALSE (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) 0 FALSE EQUALS `no duty to forward: the claim is given to the Corporation, not the employer`
-- ss 16(6), 30(5), 30(6): $1 500 each; a self-insured employer is outside them.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for each failure` FALSE EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for each failure` TRUE EQUALS 0

-- The s 30 rule, traced on the employer seat's date: 10 to 17 March is 7 days; the worker seat gives the same 7.
`the forwarding days` MEANS `days from` (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) `to` (`the last day in` (`By when must I forward this claim` TRUE (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) 0 FALSE))
#ASSERT `the forwarding days` EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `the forwarding days` EQUALS `days from` (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) `to` (`the last day in` (`By when must my employer forward my claim` TRUE (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) 0 FALSE))

`the claim as the employer sees it` MEANS
    `Claim rule facts` WITH
        `the calendar days in the prescribed period`                        IS `days from` (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) `to` (`What is the last day to make my claim` (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026))
        `the claim is given to the employer`                                IS TRUE
        `the employer is self-insured`                                      IS FALSE
        `s 30(3)(b) excuses a late claim`                                   IS FALSE
        `the calendar days to the 5th business day after the employer receives the claim` IS `the forwarding days`

-- From 3 March 2026: the claim on day 7 (10 March), forwarded on day 14 (17 March, the last day): fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 30(1), (3)(b), (5) -- a claim within 6 months, forwarded by the employer within 5 business days` `the claim as the employer sees it`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` `give the claim` 7), (EVENT `the employer` `forward a copy of the claim and a statement in the designated form to the Corporation` 14)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the employer, "s 30(5): ... maximum penalty $1 500" (forwarded on Wednesday 18 March, day 15)
#TRACE `s 30(1), (3)(b), (5) -- a claim within 6 months, forwarded by the employer within 5 business days` `the claim as the employer sees it` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the worker` DOES `give the claim` AT 7
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `forward a copy of the claim and a statement in the designated form to the Corporation` AT 15

§ `Suitable work (s 18)`

-- Mirror: the duty applies; not where the employer establishes it is not reasonably practicable; not where the worker
-- resigned after the incapacity began.
#ASSERT `Must I provide suitable work` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT (`Must I provide suitable work` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS (`Must my employer give me suitable work` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT (`Must I provide suitable work` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS (`Must my employer give me suitable work` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT (`Must I provide suitable work` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS (`Must my employer give me suitable work` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT (NOT (`Must I provide suitable work` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- s 18(4b): notice received Friday 15 May 2026: reply by Monday 15 June 2026. Mirror.
#ASSERT `By when must I reply to the worker's notice` (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 15 6 2026
#ASSERT (`By when must I reply to the worker's notice` (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026)) EQUALS (`By when must my employer answer my notice` (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026))
-- s 18(4d): a reply on 1 June 2026 gives the worker to 1 July; no reply, to 15 July. Mirror.
#ASSERT `Until when can the worker apply to the Tribunal for work` (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026) EQUALS `the worker may apply to the Tribunal no later than` (`the calendar date` 1 7 2026)
#ASSERT (`Until when can the worker apply to the Tribunal for work` (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026)) EQUALS (`By when may I apply to the Tribunal for work` (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026))
#ASSERT (`Until when can the worker apply to the Tribunal for work` (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026)) EQUALS (`By when may I apply to the Tribunal for work` (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026))
-- Mirror: s 18(4e) bars a notice given 6 months and a day after the incapacity ended.
#ASSERT (`Until when can the worker apply to the Tribunal for work` (`the calendar date` 2 4 2027) TRUE (`the calendar date` 20 4 2027) TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026)) EQUALS (`By when may I apply to the Tribunal for work` (`the calendar date` 2 4 2027) TRUE (`the calendar date` 20 4 2027) TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026))
#ASSERT `Until when can the worker apply to the Tribunal for work` (`the calendar date` 2 4 2027) TRUE (`the calendar date` 20 4 2027) TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) EQUALS `the worker cannot apply to the Tribunal under s 18(4d): s 18(4e)`

-- The s 18(4b)-(4d) rule, traced on the seats' dates: 15 May to 15 June is 31 days (both seats); 1 June to 1 July is 30.
`the reply days` MEANS `days from` (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026) `to` (`By when must I reply to the worker's notice` (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026))
#ASSERT `the reply days` EQUALS 31
#ASSERT `the reply days` EQUALS `days from` (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026) `to` (`By when must my employer answer my notice` (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026))

`the subsection (3) notice as both seats see it` MEANS
    `Subsection (3) rule facts` WITH
        `the worker may apply to the Tribunal`                           IS TRUE
        `the calendar days in the month after receipt`                   IS `the reply days`
        `the calendar days in the month after the reply`                 IS `days from` (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) `to` (`the Tribunal day in` (`Until when can the worker apply to the Tribunal for work` (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026) TRUE (`the calendar date` 1 6 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026)))
        `the calendar days in the month after the employer's month ends` IS `days from` (`the calendar date` 15 6 2026) `to` (`the Tribunal day in` (`By when may I apply to the Tribunal for work` (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026) FALSE (`the calendar date` 15 5 2026)))

-- The employer offers other suitable work on day 17 (1 June) and provides it on day 20; the worker's month to challenge it
-- (30 days, to day 47) passes unused: fulfilled. Or it refuses on day 31 (15 June, its last day); the worker's month (30
-- days, to day 61, 15 July) runs from the refusal, and she applies on day 61: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 18(4b), (4d) -- the employer must reply in writing within 1 month, and the worker may then go to the Tribunal` `the subsection (3) notice as both seats see it`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the employer` (`notify the worker in writing` `it will provide other suitable employment, with its reasons`) 17), (EVENT `the employer` `provide suitable employment` 20), (WAITUNTIL 60)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 18(4b), (4d) -- the employer must reply in writing within 1 month, and the worker may then go to the Tribunal` `the subsection (3) notice as both seats see it`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the employer` (`notify the worker in writing` `it refuses, with its grounds`) 31), (EVENT `the worker` `apply to the Tribunal for an order to provide employment` 61)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- s 18(1) from the employer seat's answer: the duty applies, and is discharged by providing the work.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 18(1), (2) -- the pre-injury employer must provide suitable employment` (`Must I provide suitable work` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the employer` `provide suitable employment` 20)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 18(1), (2) -- the pre-injury employer must provide suitable employment` (`Must I provide suitable work` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 100)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: PARTY the employer MUST provide suitable employment, still open (the duty applies and no work has been provided)
#TRACE `s 18(1), (2) -- the pre-injury employer must provide suitable employment` (`Must my employer give me suitable work` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

§ `Ending the employment (s 20)`

#ASSERT `Must I give notice before ending this worker's employment` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT (`Must I give notice before ending this worker's employment` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS (`Must my employer give me notice before ending my employment` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT (`Must I give notice before ending this worker's employment` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS (`Must my employer give me notice before ending my employment` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `What is the earliest day I may end the employment` (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 29 10 2026
#ASSERT (`What is the earliest day I may end the employment` (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026)) EQUALS (`What is the earliest day my employment can end` (`the calendar date` 1 10 2026))

§ `This worker's benefits, and damages`

#ASSERT `Is this worker a seriously injured worker` 36 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `a seriously injured worker (s 21(2))`
#ASSERT (`Is this worker a seriously injured worker` 36 0 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS (`Am I a seriously injured worker` 36 0 TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT (`Is this worker a seriously injured worker` 40 0 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS (`Am I a seriously injured worker` 40 0 FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Until when can this worker get weekly payments` FALSE (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 14 5 1990) FALSE 0 804 TRUE EQUALS `weekly payments may be paid up to and including` (`the calendar date` 28 2 2028)
#ASSERT (`Until when can this worker get weekly payments` FALSE (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 14 5 1990) FALSE 0 804 TRUE) EQUALS (`Until when can I get weekly payments` FALSE (`the calendar date` 3 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 14 5 1990) FALSE 0 804 TRUE)
#ASSERT (`Until when can this worker get weekly payments` FALSE (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 7 1960) TRUE 840 804 TRUE) EQUALS (`Until when can I get weekly payments` FALSE (`the calendar date` 2 3 2026) (`the calendar date` 1 7 1960) TRUE 840 804 TRUE)
-- s 72: 34% physical: no damages; 35%: damages may be awarded. Mirror.
#ASSERT `Can damages be awarded against me` 34 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no damages may be awarded against the employer (s 72(1))`
#ASSERT (`Can damages be awarded against me` 34 0 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS (`May I sue my employer` 34 0 TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT (`Can damages be awarded against me` 35 0 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS (`May I sue my employer` 35 0 TRUE FALSE)
-- s 100: notice received 10 March 2026: apply by 10 April 2026. Mirror.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to the Tribunal for review` (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) EQUALS `the calendar date` 10 4 2026
#ASSERT (`By when must I apply to the Tribunal for review` (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026)) EQUALS (`By when must I apply to the Tribunal` (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026))
-- The s 100(1) rule, traced on the employer seat's date: 10 March to 10 April 2026 is 31 days; the employer applies on
-- the last of them.
`the review days` MEANS `days from` (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026) `to` (`By when must I apply to the Tribunal for review` (`the calendar date` 10 3 2026))
#ASSERT `the review days` EQUALS 31
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 100(1) -- the applicant may apply to the Tribunal within 1 month after notice of the decision` `the employer` `the review days`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the employer` `apply to the Tribunal for review of the decision` 31)) EQUALS FULFILLED
